    "description": "Natural Gas Pipeline Company of America is a large interstate natural gas transmission and storage system. The asset serves producers, utilities, marketers, and industrial users through an asset-heavy, predominantly fee-based transportation and storage model. ArcLight stated in 2025 that NGPL includes about 9,100 miles of pipeline, more than one million horsepower of compression, and approximately 288 Bcf of working gas storage. The scale of the system makes it one of the larger gas infrastructure platforms in North America. ArcLight announced in May 2025 that, after acquiring Brookfield's remaining 25% interest, it would become NGPL's largest owner with a 62.5% economic interest alongside operator Kinder Morgan's 37.5% interest.",
